			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831541">
									

<p>Hi! Please note that I am not the most experienced user and am not qualified to give Greenlights. Please reach out to veteran authors and critters for some more informed crit.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">here's&nbsp;the&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">wow&nbsp;look&nbsp;at&nbsp;that</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I find the basic tenets of this idea very intriguing. The idea of a bonsai tree infecting the noosphere (collective human thought) is suitably mysterious and has great imagery potential. However, I believe that you'll find more success, both in the idea forums and the mainlist, if you can simplify your idea as much as possible. When I was having similar issues, this guide helped a lot: <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/yourjouney-part-1">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/yourjouney-part-1</a></p>
<p>Another issue I have is that the exact nature of this anomaly seems to be a bit shaky. Here are some questions that I have that might inspire the development process:<br />
Bonsai trees typically represent peace or tranquillity. What causes this one to be a symbol of the exact opposite?<br />
There are multiple issues with the entire world instantly becoming aware of this phenomenon. What if everyone has this image in their minds, but cannot place it and typically don't pay it much mind?<br />
Bonsai trees are tightly controlled by their gardeners to take on certain shapes and inspire certain feelings. What does the nature of this tree say about the person who grew it?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I believe this has promise. If you receive the necessary greenlights, please reach out to me with a draft. Have a good day!</p>

