														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831563">
									

<p>Hello there! I saw 'Collective Unconscious' and I just&#8230;had to swing by and give my thoughts.</p>
<p>So.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Let's&nbsp;do&nbsp;it!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Let's&nbsp;do&nbsp;it!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First, the <strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>. I <em>want</em> to like it, what with the imagery of a tree and its root connecting to and reaching throughout all of humanity's subconscious and such, but so far, all it does is just&#8230;make people see it in their heads and then make them feel dread.</p>
<p>As for the <strong>Central Narrative</strong>, I'm similarly not very impressed.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The apartment, officially the containment cell for the anomaly, looked to be lived in, but beyond writings and personal belongings of the tenant, there are no records of residence.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels tacked on and like it was added solely to attempt to add a sense of mystery and nothing else. It's never elaborated upon and it's mentioned and dropped immediately.</p>
<p>There are also some bits that contradict each other.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the tree is supposed to be representative of a universal dread,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I like this bit, but other than the imagery of roots that obviously allude to burrowing throughout the Collective Unconscious, this, too, fails to go anywhere.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I'm not looking to write something scary or unsettling. I just want to make something that's curious.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If it's meant to be scary or unsettling, then why dread?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The problem is that I don't want to be overt about it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Unfortunately, it is very overt.</p>
<p>And that ends my crit. I do apologize if this was overly harsh.</p>
<p>There's some neat imagery in here, but sadly, not much else to go off of.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In summary, the tree is supposed to be representative of a universal dread, while the tenant, seemingly untrackable, is like an unobtainable goal.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence alone was my favorite part of this entire forum post. Especialy 'dread' and 'like an unobtainable goal' got my attention.</p>
<p>I recommend peeking a little more into Carl Jung's studies on psychoanalysis if you really want to make an SCP based off a symbol in the Collective Unconscious.</p>
<p>Anywho, I hope I helped and I bid you a lovely day! :D</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

